      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I think we should replace the paths with ones that are relative to the ec root dir, so it doesn\u0027t matter if it is used in the chroot or outside.\n\nInteresting! In the EC file I see `directory` has the full path, while `file` is relative:\n\n```\n        \"directory\": \"/home/agrandi/chromiumos/src/platform/ec\",\n        \"file\": \"util/iteflash.c\"\n```\n\nIn the Zephyr file, both `directory` and `file` are absolute.\n\n```\n  \"directory\": \"/home/agrandi/chromiumos/src/platform/ec/build/zephyr/herobrine/build-rw\",\n  \"file\": \"/home/agrandi/chromiumos/src/platform/ec/build/zephyr/herobrine/modules/ec/common/virtual_battery.c\"\n```\n\nIs it mandatory for `directory` to remain absolute? Would that break the use inside the `chroot`?\n\nUpdating all paths except for `directory` is possible, but probably more complicated. I wonder if there will ever be a use for the `compile_commands.json` inside the chroot.\n\n\n\u003e Oops, it looks like we aren\u0027t converting the /opt/coreboot-sdk/bin/arm-eabi-gcc in this example, nor in the EC commands case.\n\nDo you think this is going to break things? The EC auto completion seems to work okay. What should we replace this with?",
      "parentUuid": "80c99e4e_2f5cbf36",
      "revId": "4dc21bd68b3bca1754dc5e2a15053665c56a66cb",
